From aea486b86ddf81d88c07e631ad131902597b4dec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Instinct <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:01:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add opt-in BS-Roformer-SW six-stem separation engine

STEMDECK_SEPARATION_ENGINE=roformer-sw runs BS-Roformer-SW through
audio-separator in its own worker and writes the same six stems.
Default stays demucs htdemucs_6s. No fallback between engines, no use or
download without STEMDECK_ROFORMER_SW_ACCEPT=1 (the weights have no
stated licence), failures name the engine and model.

- audio-separator range 0.38-0.45 declared and locked (Intel macOS keeps
  its torch 2.2 / numpy<2 pins and gets no audio-separator, as before).
- Stems keep their relative levels: per-stem normalisation is replaced by
  float32 output plus one common gain.
- torch.load is forced to weights_only for the unverified checkpoint.
